# Cloudflare Pages: serve the SPA shell for per-project deep links.
# The site is a single index.html with no server-side routing, so any
# /projets/<slug> URL (shared link, bookmark, reload while a project is
# open) must return index.html with a 200 — the client-side JS then reads
# the path and opens the matching project. Everything else (/, assets,
# images) is served normally by Pages' static handler.
# The target is "/" and NOT "/index.html": Pages' pretty URLs answer
# /index.html with a 308 to /, and a 200 rewrite onto a redirect ends in
# the 404 page (refreshing /projets/e-9e gave a 404 in October 2026).

